#30201
Southwest Meadow~
A wide meadow of tall grass and yellow flowers fills the far southwest
corner of the land, hemmed in by brown rock to the south and west. Some of
the flower heads spin on their stalks with no wind to turn them, and now
and then one lifts free and whirls overhead like a top before settling
again. It is a quiet, forgotten corner, and the only trampled path leads
east toward the woods.
