#30217
The Tangled Woods~
Dense trees crowd close on every side, their branches knotted overhead into
a dim green roof. Paths wind away in all four directions between the
trunks, and the only sounds are rustling leaves and the creak of old wood.
Snapped spear-shafts and blue-dyed scraps of hide lie half-buried in the
leaf litter, dropped by whatever hunts these woods in pairs.
