#30221
Forest Stream~
A narrow stream threads through the trees, chattering over pebbles and
pooling in quiet, fern-hung basins. Mossy stepping stones make for an easy
crossing, though now and then the water bulges and a scaly head breaks the
surface to spit a ball of fire before sinking again. Scorch marks blister
the stones. Cool air rises off the current, and paths lead away in all four
directions.
