Moblin Hollow~
A shallow hollow among the trees is strewn with trampled grass, chewed
bones and the ashes of a cold campfire. Crude spears lean against a fallen
log, and the forest is noisy with snapping twigs and distant, piggish
grunts. The ground is churned by broad, clawed feet. Paths climb out of the
hollow in all four directions.
