#30246
Candlemaker's Dead End~
The forest trail runs out in a small hollow walled in by trees and a
shoulder of grey rock. In the rock face a low cave mouth glows with a warm,
steady flicker, and the smell of tallow and wick smoke drifts out on the
still air, where a merchant sells candles and bait to those who come this
far. The woods beyond are too thick to pass, so the only way back is west.
