#30247
The Coast's Lonely Ledge~
Rough grass runs down to the eastern shore, where the sea washes against
tumbled rocks. Just offshore a small flat ledge of stone sits alone above
the waves, separated from the land by a strip of water too wide to step and
narrow enough to bridge with a ladder. A faint red glow pulses on the ledge
like a heartbeat. The coast path leads north and south.
