#30248
The Graveyard's Southern Fence~
Weathered headstones lean in crooked rows behind a low, crumbling wall,
their names long since rubbed away by wind and rain. The grass grows thin
and grey, a cold mist clings to the ground, and now and then a pale shape
drifts across the stones and is gone. To the south the land drops to dark
water and a small stone landing for a raft, and open country runs on to the
east and north.
