#30252
Riverside Cave~
A swift green river cuts through the woods here, its banks lined with reeds
and smooth grey stones. Across a stretch of grass a low cave mouth is set
into a rocky bank, and the whiff of black powder drifting from inside marks
a merchant of bombs and arrows. A finned head rises from the water now and
then, spits a glowing ball, and sinks. Trails follow the river north and
south.
