#30254
Lake Hylia, Western Reeds~
Tall reeds rustle along the western edge of Lake Hylia, and the water slaps
gently against a muddy bank. A finned head sometimes rises out of the reeds
to spit fire, then sinks. A lone, scraggly bush stands somewhat apart from
the rest, dry and brittle as tinder, and a merchant's painted price mark
shows on a stone among its roots. The shore curves away east, and a path
climbs south.
