#30255
Lake Hylia, South Shore~
Broad blue water stretches north as far as the eye can see, sparkling under
an open sky, its far shore lost in haze. Ripples spread from somewhere out
in the deep, where something finned rises and sinks. Near the bank a single
dense bush grows by itself, dry and crackling in the sun, and the ground
beneath it gives off a faint warm glow. The shore runs on east and west.
