Lake Hylia Sand Bar~
A pale sand bar runs along the lake's edge, the sand rippled and pocked
with burrow holes from which a red spinning thing sometimes bores up. The
water laps in long slow waves, and a lonely bush stands at the edge of the
grass, brittle and brown, with coin-sized footprints worn around it. Paths
lead north along the water, south toward the fields and west along the
shore.
