Boulder Meadow~
Rolling green meadow is broken by heavy grey boulders that lie half sunk in
the turf. One sits a little apart from the others, as if it had been rolled
there by some great hand and might be rolled away again by a strong enough
one, and a draught breathes up from the earth at its base. Spat stones lie
about the grass. Trails lead off to the north, east and south.
