skitter down the slopes at every gust. The soil is scuffed with the paired
prints of long-legged hopping things, blue lichen crushed into each one.
Tucked under one ledge is a dark cave mouth that smells of black powder,
where a merchant trades bombs and arrows. Paths run north, east and west.
