littered with snapped arrows and gnawed bones. One bush near the path looks
unusually dry, its leaves curled and ready to catch the smallest spark, and
a sweet, bitter smell of medicine drifts from beneath it. Red-dyed hide
hangs on a thornbush. The thicket opens to the north, the south and the
west.
