The Eastern Dock~
A weathered wooden dock juts out from the grassy bank over open water, its
planks bleached grey and its posts green with weed. Water stretches away
northward toward a hazy green spit where a stone gate stands, too far to
swim but easy going on a raft. Spat stones lie scattered on the planks.
Behind the dock the meadow rolls off to the east.
