#30263
Eastern Cliffs~
The land ends abruptly at a line of rocky cliffs above the sea, and salt
spray drifts up on a cool wind. Gulls wheel and cry overhead while waves
boom against the rocks far below. Blue-grey stones lie flung across the
clifftop where something stout spits them at passers-by. A grassy track
runs along the clifftop to the north and south.
