The Graveyard, Lower Rows~
The southern rows of the graveyard are crowded with weathered headstones,
their names long worn away and their tops green with lichen. Dead grass
crackles underfoot, and a cold mist clings to the ground between the
graves, gathering now and then into a pale, drifting shape that fades when
looked at squarely. The paths lead north into the older graves, south along
the fence and east toward the living lands.
