The Graveyard Gate~
Here the graves thin out toward the edge of the burial ground, where a gap
in the boundary lets travellers pass. The headstones nearest the gate lean
outward as if to see who comes and goes, and the earth before each one is
disturbed, as though touching a grave wakes whatever sleeps beneath. The
mist gathers thickest by the gap. Ways lead north, south, east and west.
