stained by old water. Near its base the stone is cracked and flaking, and a
faint herbal scent of boiled roots drifts out of the gaps, as if a medicine
woman kept shop behind a wall that a bomb could open. A narrow crevice to
the north wants a ladder, and the land opens to the west.
