Deep grooves are worn into the floor between the corners, where blocks of
spiked iron sit in shallow recesses, polished bright by endless sliding at
whoever crosses their line. The ceiling is low and hung with roosting
stains where bats flit. A spiderweb of cracks runs through the east wall,
and open doorways lead north and south.
