Raised blocks stand in a checkerboard across this wide chamber, and every
lane between them is choked with bones, shields and helmets green with age,
some of which climb to their feet and hop toward the living. The clatter of
loose ribs underfoot sets echoes running along the walls. A heavy shutter
guards the west doorway, and the south wall is split by a ragged crack.
