A broad moat cuts across this chamber, its dark water lapping softly
against a narrow causeway of stone that bends toward the far doors, a
crossing too narrow to fight on comfortably. The smell of wet moss is
thick, and boomerang splinters drift in the water. A locked door with a
brass keyhole stands to the north, and a heavy shutter seals the east
