Four stone lions crouch at the corners of this square hall, their blank
eyes fixed on the middle of the floor. The paving between them is cracked
in a starburst pattern, as if something heavy fell there long ago. An open
arch leads south, a heavy shutter seals the north, and a locked door stands
to the east.
