Level 9: The Cartographer's Vault~
Dust spins in a slow circle across the floor of this sealed eastern vault,
as if stirred by an endless breath, and the walls are scored by the orbit
of many small eyes. Faded lines are etched into the stone like old
surveyors' marks. There are no doorways at all, only cracked and weakened
sections in the north, south and west walls.
