#30658
Across the Narrow Water~
This rocky ledge lies just beyond a channel of water too wide to step and
too narrow to bother swimming; a traveller with a stepladder can bridge it
in a moment. The ledge is quiet, sheltered from the coast wind by a
shoulder of rock, and littered with gull feathers and driftwood around a
faint red glow, as if a heart had been left here to keep warm.
~
