#30680
A Merchant's Cave~
Two fires light a dry, low-ceilinged cave where three wares are laid out in
a neat row on the bare floor. A price in rupees is painted on the stone
beneath each one, and above them a cheerful scrawl reads BUY SOMETHIN',
WILL YA! There is no haggling. The merchant chose the spot carefully: close
enough to the road for trade, far enough from it for safety.
