#30753
The Lost Hills~
Brown hills rise and fall here, each fold of ground so like the last that
the eye loses its place among them. The trail climbs north toward the high
peaks between banks of loose scree, and paths wander off east and west
along the slope. On a flat stone by the trail someone has scratched: GO UP,
UP, THE MOUNTAIN AHEAD. Loose rocks bound down from above now and then.
~
